BT 1 0 0 1 0 99 Tm 12 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Three of the largest open problems in physics -- dark matter, dark energy, and the vacuum catastrophe -- are treated here) Tj T* (as manifestations of a single mechanism: the Wike Coherence Law, C = C_0 ) Tj /F3 9 Tf (exp\(-alpha ) Tj /F1 9 Tf (gamma_eff\). Dark matter is not a) Tj T* (particle but a residual coherent vacuum state that persists in low-decoherence regions. The vacuum catastrophe \(the) Tj T* (10^122 discrepancy between QFT-predicted and observed vacuum energy\) is closed by cosmic decoherence: exp\(-276\) ~) Tj T* -0.114 Tw (10^-120. Dark energy is the surviving fraction of vacuum coherence after that suppression, and its observed evolution \(DESI) Tj T* 0 Tw (2024\) follows from the gamma_eff dependence of the exponential. The dark matter-dark energy coincidence problem, the) Tj T* (radial acceleration relation, and the baryonic Tully-Fisher relation all reduce to algebraic consequences of the coherence) Tj T* (law. No new particles, no fine-tuning, and no free parameters beyond those already fixed by dimensional analysis \(Paper) Tj T* (62\) and universal constant derivations \(Paper 100\).) Tj T* ET
